<title>USA: TABLE - American Home Products Q2 shr rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - American Home Products Q2 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>MADISON, N.J. 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended June 30</p>
<p>			     1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.71		    $0.62</p>
<p> Net			459,092		  391,277</p>
<p> Revs		   3,499,758		3,489,821</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 645,578		  633,937</p>
<p>	   6 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.61		    $1.39</p>
<p> Net		    1,035,769		  880,640</p>
<p> Revs		   7,102,777		7,136,635</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 644,042		  632,155</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: Full company name is American Home Products Corp.</p>
<p>Pharmaceuticals sales rose 9 percent to $1.93 billion.</p>
<p>Agriculture products sales rose 3 percent to $792.4 million.</p>
<p>Consumer health care products sales fell 2 percent to $445,713 million.</p>
<p>Pharmaceutical and agricultural sales worldwide were hurt by unfavorable effects of foreign exchange.</p>
</text>
